WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.850
Jordan has experience helping patients.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.190
But the next move isn't just another front-desk job.

3
00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.811
Jordan wants to help run a practice.

4
00:00:13.621 --> 00:00:18.391
So the search starts with a clear direction, and the kind of work that would actually fit.

5
00:00:22.543 --> 00:00:24.173
This role looks promising.

6
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:28.093
The pay and direction make sense.

7
00:00:28.503 --> 00:00:32.233
But there's a catch: Jordan hasn't confirmed the Epic experience the employer requires.

8
00:00:40.718 --> 00:00:44.454
Instead of guessing, Jordan checks the record: scheduling, referrals,

9
00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:47.608
insurance work, and a problem solved at the clinic.

10
00:00:48.158 --> 00:00:50.808
Real experience, with limits worth knowing.

11
00:00:54.806 --> 00:00:58.436
With those facts, Sojourner prepares a resume for this opportunity.

12
00:00:58.966 --> 00:01:01.976
Its truth check helps keep unverified experience out.

13
00:01:02.386 --> 00:01:05.576
Jordan can put a stronger application together without making things up.

14
00:01:07.548 --> 00:01:11.478
The decision stays Jordan's.

15
00:01:11.728 --> 00:01:14.598
Sojourner keeps the opportunity, the resume, and the next step in one place.

16
00:01:15.068 --> 00:01:17.558
It doesn't apply to employers on Jordan's behalf.

17
00:01:23.472 --> 00:01:26.362
A clearer direction. An honest assessment.

18
00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:29.322
And one next step that Jordan chose deliberately.

19
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.400
Sojourner. Make the next move count.

